# Commit identities seen before this account was the only one.
#
# The early history was committed as `ares` and `ubuntu` on throwaway addresses.
# Those names are not GitHub accounts, so GitHub listed them as separate greyed
# contributors beside the real one. Mapping them here folds the old commits into
# zxsmind without rewriting a single commit id: the canonical name and address
# win, the old ones after it are what get replaced.
#
# `git log --use-mailmap` resolves this; GitHub reads the same file when it
# attributes a commit.

zxsmind <zxsmind@gmail.com> <ubuntu@ares.athena.local>
zxsmind <zxsmind@gmail.com> <ubuntu@athena.local>
